-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
indic-nlp-library and urduhack (IndicNLPTokenizer)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
crates/pyroid-core/src/filters/indic.rs and indic_tables.rs port datatrove's
IndicNLPTokenizer, that is indic-nlp-library 0.92,
https://github.com/anoopkunchukuttan/indic_nlp_library (trivial_tokenize,
sentence_split with is_acronym_abbvr's non-breaking phrases, langinfo's script
ranges and danda languages, and the Sinhala-to-Devanagari map), and, for Urdu
sentences, urduhack 1.0.3, https://github.com/urduhack/urduhack (the rule-based
splitter of tokenization/eos.py and its two word lists), which
indic-nlp-library calls for "ur". indic_tables.rs is generated from the two
libraries themselves by crates/pyroid-core/src/filters/generate_indic_tables.py;
it also holds the str.isnumeric() sets of CPython 3.11-3.15's Unicode databases
and the \p{Lu} and WhitespaceTokenizer sentence-pattern classes as the regex
module matches them (see "Data derived from CPython and Unicode" above). The
differential tests (crates/pyroid-core/tests/filters_indic.rs,
filters_data/indic/record.py, and the IndicNLP fuzzer and word lists of
filters_data/oracle.py) derive from the same releases;
filters_data/indic/golden.jsonl and filters_data/multilingual/golden-indic-*.jsonl
record what these libraries return on pyroid's own test texts.

Each of these files but the .jsonl recordings carries a header naming
indic-nlp-library 0.92 (MIT), © Anoop Kunchukuttan, and urduhack 1.0.3 (MIT),
© Urdu Hack, alongside datatrove 0.10.1 (Apache-2.0), © HuggingFace (see
above), e.g. indic.rs's "Derived from indic-nlp-library 0.92 (MIT), © Anoop
Kunchukuttan, urduhack 1.0.3 (MIT), © Urdu Hack, and datatrove 0.10.1
(Apache-2.0), © HuggingFace; modified."

