rouge-score and NLTK (pyroid.metrics ROUGE)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The ROUGE port (crates/pyroid-core/src/metrics/rouge/, crates/pyroid-py/src/metrics/rouge.rs,
python/pyroid/metrics/rouge_scorer.py, scoring.py, tokenizers.py, tokenize.py
and their .pyi stubs, crates/pyroid-core/tests/metrics_rouge.rs and
crates/pyroid-core/tests/metrics_data/rouge_*) is a derivative work of
rouge-score 0.1.2,
https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/rouge:

    Copyright 2022 The rouge_score Authors.

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

Each ported file carries the header "Derived from rouge-score 0.1.2
(Apache-2.0), © The rouge_score Authors; modified." scoring.BootstrapAggregator is ported
verbatim (it calls numpy, which is not bundled).

The Porter stemmer (crates/pyroid-core/src/metrics/rouge/porter.rs) is a port of
nltk/stem/porter.py from NLTK 3.10.4, https://www.nltk.org, in its default
NLTK_EXTENSIONS mode, the stemmer rouge-score uses:

    Copyright (C) 2001-2026 NLTK Project

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

The algorithm is Martin Porter's, "An algorithm for suffix stripping",
Program 14.3 (1980): 130-137.

